  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-11T11:38:43.304Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Everyone knows about the Twitch and Youtube platforms, but ecologically it's a disaster...\nThis is why it is important to find alternatives to these community platforms.\nPlaying multiplayer video games consumes much less than watching a video stream.\nSo the idea would be to create a web platform or apps that would allow us to connect to a world by downloading all the assets beforehand and the player would be connected to the streamer's camera.\nLike the desktop version of VRCHAT with only spectator features.\nThe viewer would see what the streamer wants to show him, the textures would not need to be downloaded every time he wants to see the stream.\nThe only thing that would consume internet data would be the management of the movements of the objects and players.\nA good way to separate from twitch and youtube.\nWhile remaining ecologically responsible.\n=======================\nI would love to talk directly to a developer, as I have a clear idea of how to implement this system.\nSo if you want to discuss it, contact me in private message or by discord.",
